From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hyunchul Lee <hyc.lee@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:42:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] ntfs: avoid overflow when limiting attribute read length

commit 4b927614d92d7326f265d22b50ba7b4a33966e48 upstream.

ntfs_inode_attr_pread() limits a read to the attribute size using
pos + count. A large count can overflow the signed sum and bypass
the attribute EOF boundary check. Compare count with isize - pos
instead, after validating pos, so the read length limit cannot wrap.

Fixes: af0db57d4293 ("ntfs: update inode operations")
Signed-off-by: Hyunchul Lee <hyc.lee@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Baolin Liu <liubaolin@kylinos.cn>
Signed-off-by: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>
[Hades: backported to 7.3.4. There ntfs_inode_attr_pread() takes
 ni->mrec_lock, where mainline takes mrec_ni->mrec_lock since the
 named-stream support (48996054b706), which Hades does not take; the
 hunk in it is rebuilt on 7.3.4's lines. The change is the same.]
---
 fs/ntfs/inode.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/ntfs/inode.c b/fs/ntfs/inode.c
index ee4c3ad2c453..cbef6e6ad94c 100644
--- a/fs/ntfs/inode.c
+++ b/fs/ntfs/inode.c
@@ -3619,7 +3619,7 @@ s64 ntfs_inode_attr_pread(struct inode *vi, s64 pos, s64 count, u8 *buf)
 		mutex_unlock(&ni->mrec_lock);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
-	if (pos + count > isize)
+	if (count > isize - pos)
 		count = isize - pos;
 
 	if (!NInoNonResident(ni)) {
